# Nougat extraction stub

Paper: Ruigrok et al. 2022, "In vitro dose effect relationships of
actinium-225- and lutetium-177-labeled PSMA-I&T", Eur J Nucl Med Mol
Imaging 49:3627–3638. DOI: 10.1007/s00259-022-05821-w.

## Provenance

**Canonical parser status:** Marker MD for this DOI is NOT present in
`/data/stevens/lucid100_merged/by_paper/` or
`/data/stevens/lucid-corpus-extracted/` on uicgpu (verified 2026-06-23
via `ssh uicgpu ls | grep`).

**Canonical text used for this replication:**
- `paper.pdf` — Open Access (CC-BY) source PDF, stored at top level of
  this replication directory.
- `paper.txt` — `pdftotext -layout paper.pdf paper.txt` on the top-level
  PDF; this is the canonical text source for the 2026-06-23 re-pass
  (all C7–C19 claim scripts read numeric values from it).

**Nougat status:** not run for this paper. Under the LUCID pipeline this
would be a supplementary extraction; the primary extraction chain is
Marker → pdftotext fallback. Since Marker output does not exist on
uicgpu for this DOI and pdftotext-layout was sufficient to extract every
numeric value from the Results section and Tables 2–3 needed for the
12-claim re-pass, running Nougat was not required.

If a future pass needs Nougat-flavored math-LaTeX extraction (for
example to re-derive the fitted equations symbolically), invoke:

```
nougat paper.pdf --out ./extraction --recompute
```

on a host with a compatible GPU. Output should land at
`extraction/paper.mmd`.

## Numeric ground truth (from paper.txt)

The following values are the paper's stated numbers used in the
replication (all quoted verbatim from `paper.txt` Results section and
Tables 2–3):

- α(Ac-225) = 0.67 ± 0.06 Gy⁻¹
- α(Lu-177) = 0.16 ± 0.01 Gy⁻¹
- RBE = 4.2 ± 0.46
- Biological t½ = 2.3 h, plateau 41 %
- Uptake fraction = 1.88 %AA / 1e5 cells (avg 1h+3h Lu)
- Membrane / internal split = 0.24 / 0.76
- Cross-dose S-value Lu-177 = 1.13E-6 Gy/(Bq·s)
- IC₅₀(Ac-225) = 1.53E-8 M; IC₅₀(Lu-177) = 2.61E-8 M
- Peak foci Ac = 18.1 ± 7.4 at 16 h; Peak foci Lu = 14.3 ± 6.4 at 0 h
- Table 3 average-dim doses used verbatim as fit-input dose grid.

See `paper.txt` at top level for the primary text source and
`code/replicate_lucid.py` (constants block) for the machine-readable
extraction into the pipeline.
